# Replaces .gitignore for the EAS build archive -- when this file exists,
# eas-cli reads it INSTEAD of every .gitignore in the repo (see
# eas-cli/build/vcs/local.js, Ignore.initIgnoreAsync). It exists for one
# reason: .gitignore line 34 is `*.db`, which matches the bundled corpus
# at apps/mobile/assets/db/quran.db. Without this file that asset is dropped
# from the upload and every device check fails on a database that is not there
# -- the ~5 MB upload the README warns about.
#
# Because .gitignore stops applying, everything heavy or private has to be
# re-listed here. Anything added to .gitignore later must be mirrored here or
# it starts getting uploaded to Expo.
#
# .git and node_modules are ignored by eas-cli itself and need no entry.

# --- Build output and caches -------------------------------------------------
.expo/
.turbo/
dist/
build/
coverage/
.next/
*.tsbuildinfo
.mypy_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Python virtualenv (1.3 GB of it) ----------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/

# --- Native projects: expo prebuild output, regenerated on the builder -------
/apps/mobile/android/
/apps/mobile/ios/

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.keystore
*.mobileprovision

# --- Third-party reference data: licensed elsewhere, never ours to upload ----
/packages/scraper/.refdata/
/temp/

# --- Corpus databases -------------------------------------------------------
# Everything except the one the app actually bundles. Listed by path rather
# than as `*.db` + a negation: `ignore`'s exception handling is documented as
# inconsistent with git's, so the asset stays outside any ignore rule instead
# of relying on `!` to rescue it.
/apps/web/quran.db
/packages/scraper/quran.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db.bak*
/packages/data/*.db

# --- Local scratch ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.claude/
.superpowers/
.impeccable/
